{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/Content-swift.enum","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/Content-swift.enum\/SyllabicGroup","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/Content-swift.enum\/SyllabicGroup\/Group-swift.struct"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The elision symbol connecting this syllable to the following text.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/Content-swift.enum\/SyllabicGroup\/Group-swift.struct\/elision","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property","title":"elision","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"elision","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLElisionV","text":"MXLElision","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLyricV7ContentO13SyllabicGroupV0F0V7elisionAA10MXLElisionVvp"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"elision","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLElisionV","text":"MXLElision","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/content-swift.enum\/syllabicgroup\/group-swift.struct\/elision"]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLElision":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLElision","title":"MXLElision","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLElision","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLElision","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlelision","abstract":[{"text":"The elision type represents an elision between lyric syllables. The text content specifies the symbol used to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"display the elision. Common values are a no-break space (Unicode 00A0), an underscore (Unicode 005F), or an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"undertie (Unicode 203F). If the text content is empty, the smufl attribute is used to specify the symbol to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use. Its value is a SMuFL canonical glyph name that starts with lyrics. The SMuFL attribute is ignored if the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elision glyph is already specified by the text content. If neither text content nor a smufl attribute are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"present, the elision glyph is application-specific.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric/Content-swift.enum/SyllabicGroup/Group-swift.struct":{"title":"MXLLyric.Content.SyllabicGroup.Group","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Group"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/content-swift.enum\/syllabicgroup\/group-swift.struct","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/Content-swift.enum\/SyllabicGroup\/Group-swift.struct","abstract":[{"text":"The elision and optional syllabic hyphenation type that precede a further syllable of elided lyric text.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Group"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric/Content-swift.enum":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One of the alternatives for Lyric."}],"title":"MXLLyric.Content","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/Content-swift.enum","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/content-swift.enum","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Content"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The lyric type represents text underlays for lyrics. Two text elements that are not separated by an elision","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element are part of the same syllable, but may have different text formatting. The MusicXML XSD is more strict","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than the DTD in enforcing this by disallowing a second syllabic element unless preceded by an elision element.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The lyric number indicates multiple lines, though a name can be used as well. Common name examples are verse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and chorus.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLLyric","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric/Content-swift.enum/SyllabicGroup":{"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SyllabicGroup"}],"title":"MXLLyric.Content.SyllabicGroup","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/content-swift.enum\/syllabicgroup","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SyllabicGroup"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/Content-swift.enum\/SyllabicGroup","abstract":[{"text":"An elided continuation of a lyric syllable, consisting of an optional elision-and-syllabic marker paired","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with additional text.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric/Content-swift.enum/SyllabicGroup/Group-swift.struct/elision":{"title":"elision","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"elision"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLElisionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLElision"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/content-swift.enum\/syllabicgroup\/group-swift.struct\/elision","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/Content-swift.enum\/SyllabicGroup\/Group-swift.struct\/elision","abstract":[{"text":"The elision symbol connecting this syllable to the following text.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"}}}